    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d26">

                <pb facs="0112" n="32" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg32"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A5/612: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-01-13T23:00:00+09:00">January 13,
                            1936—11 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 13—11:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>11. For Davis, London. My 10, January 13, 6 p.m.<anchor n="20" xml:id="d26-f1"/>
                        Hirota<anchor n="21" xml:id="d26-f2"/> tonight confirmed to me personally
                    and definitely that he had won out in his contest with the Navy over immediate
                    withdrawal of the Japanese delegation from London. He said that while Admiral
                    Nagano might return to Tokyo he hoped and expected that Ambassador Nagai<anchor
                        n="22" xml:id="d26-f3"/> would remain in the Conference.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d26-f1" n="20" xml:id="d26-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d26-f2" n="21" xml:id="d26-f2-content">
                <p>Koki Hirota, Japanese Minister for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d26-f3" n="22" xml:id="d26-f3-content">
                <p>Matsuzo Nagai, Japanese Ambassador in the United Kingdom and delegate to the
                    Naval Conference.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
